\ Functional words over arrays: find-first / any? / all? / each / flat-map /
\ sort-by / partition / group-by with an xt key.

\ === find-first ===========================================================
[ 1 2 3 4 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) find-first . cr             \ 2   (first match, not 4)
[ 1 3 5 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) find-first . cr               \ null
[ ] ( drop 1 ) find-first . cr                       \ null
[ "a" "bb" "ccc" ] ( size 2 = ) find-first . cr      \ bb

\ === any? / all? ===========================================================
[ 1 3 5 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) any? . cr               \ 0
[ 1 2 3 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) any? . cr               \ 1
[ ] ( drop 1 ) any? . cr                       \ 0
[ 2 4 6 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) all? . cr               \ 1
[ 2 4 5 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) all? . cr               \ 0
[ ] ( drop 0 ) all? . cr                       \ 1   (vacuously true)

\ === each ==================================================================
0 to total
[ 1 2 3 4 ] ( ^total | total + to total ) each
total . cr                                       \ 10
[ ] ( ^total | total + to total ) each
total . cr                                       \ 10  (no elements, no calls)

\ === flat-map ==============================================================
[ 1 2 3 ] ( dup 2 array ) flat-map . cr        \ [ 1 1 2 2 3 3 ]
[ 1 2 3 ] ( drop [ ] ) flat-map . cr           \ [ ]
[ 1 3 ] ( dup 1 + range ) flat-map . cr        \ [ 1 2 3 4 ]

\ === sort-by ===============================================================
[ "ccc" "a" "bb" ] ' size sort-by . cr           \ [ "a" "bb" "ccc" ]
[ 3 1 4 1 5 9 2 6 ] ' negate sort-by . cr        \ descending
[ ] ' negate sort-by . cr                        \ [ ]
[ { :n 2 } { :n 1 } ] ( :n @ ) sort-by . cr    \ frames by field

\ a symbol key reads that field, so it needs no quotation
[ { :n 3 } { :n 1 } { :n 2 } ] :n sort-by . cr   \ 1 2 3
\ an array of keys sorts by each in turn, the first primary; equal keys keep
\ input order, so :a alone leaves the two :a 1 rows as they came
[ { :a 1 :b 2 } { :a 1 :b 1 } { :a 0 :b 9 } ] [ :a :b ] sort-by . cr  \ a0 then a1b1 then a1b2
[ { :a 1 :b 2 } { :a 1 :b 1 } { :a 0 :b 9 } ] [ :a ] sort-by . cr     \ a0 then a1b2 then a1b1
[ { :a 1 } { :a 0 } ] [ ] sort-by . cr           \ no keys, order untouched
\ a mixed array takes symbols and tokens together
[ "ccc" "a" "bb" ] [ ' size ] sort-by . cr       \ [ "a" "bb" "ccc" ]

\ === partition =============================================================
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) partition swap . . cr   \ evens then odds
[ 1 3 5 ] ( 2 mod 0= ) partition swap . . cr         \ [ ] then all
[ ] ( drop 1 ) partition swap . . cr                 \ both empty

\ === group-by with an xt key ===============================================
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] ( 2 mod 0= if :even else :odd then ) group-by . cr
[ ] ( drop :x ) group-by . cr                  \ { }
[ "ant" "bee" "cow" "asp" ] ( 0 1 substring string>symbol ) group-by . cr

\ === exit inside a bare quotation ends the iteration ======================
\ (the direct-dispatch loop path: exit stops at the run floor, no frame)
[ 1 2 3 ] ( dup 2 = if drop 99 exit then 1+ ) map . cr   \ [ 2 99 4 ]
( 7 ) 2 times . . cr                                     \ 7 7
[ 1 2 3 ] ( to x x 2 = if 0 exit then x ) map . cr   \ [ 1 0 3 ] scratch frame

\ === errors ================================================================
[ { :n 1 } ] 5 sort-by                  \ (a key that is neither a symbol nor a token)

bye
